# Code Quality Rules

## No Temporary Solutions
- Always implement final, production-ready solutions
- If a temporary solution is absolutely necessary, mark it clearly with TODO and explain why
- Avoid placeholder implementations that will need to be rewritten later

## No Stub Functions
- Do not create empty function bodies or stub implementations
- Every function should have complete, working implementation
- If implementation is complex, break it into smaller, fully-implemented functions

## No Simplified Versions
- Implement the full feature as specified, not a reduced version
- Don't omit edge cases or error handling to simplify implementation
- If the full implementation is too complex for one session, clearly document what remains to be done with TODO comments

## No Fallback Functions
- Do not create fallback or backup function implementations
- Each function should have one clear, correct implementation path
- Avoid creating multiple versions of the same functionality "just in case"
- If error handling is needed, use proper error codes or exceptions, not alternative implementations

## No Original Code Creation
- Do not create new code from scratch unless explicitly requested
- Default task is to rewrite existing code from C:\coding\CPP\cossacks-revamp-2017-master\src\Main executable
- We are rewriting the original game code to OpenGL x64 C++
- Always base implementations on the original game's logic and structure
- Only add new functionality when specifically asked to do so
- Preserve original game behavior and mechanics unless told otherwise

## Confirmation Protocol
- Always end responses with "Yes sir" to confirm that all rules have been remembered and applied in the implementation
- This confirms adherence to: no temporary solutions, no stub functions, no simplified versions, no fallback functions, and proper use of original game code as the base

